{
  "schema": "reach-rules/v0",
  "note": "facts: what the tool looks for in first-party (app) classes. verdicts: how verdict.py combines facts. A condition is a list of fact ids that must all hold; '!id' means the fact must be absent. Order: reachable_if -> unreachable_if -> unknown_if -> otherwise. Pseudo facts from the call graph: sink (a vulnerable method is reachable through ordinary call edges), sink_weak (reachable only through Object.equals/hashCode/toString dispatch or JDK callbacks), sinks_missing (none of the vulnerable methods exist in the analysed jars), package (any method of the vulnerable library is reachable). Optional per-verdict 'info': fact ids shown in the report for reference only; they never decide the verdict.",
